    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573-a1">

                <pb facs="0575" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg477"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">M Long to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 19th instant, inclosing for the information of this
                    Department a copy of a dispatch from the Ambassador of the United States at
                    Paris, inclosing a copy of a letter from the “Société Générale de Transports
                    Maritimes à Vapeur” concerning the towing of the disabled steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bretagne</hi> into the port of Bahia by the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chicago.</hi></p>
                <p>A copy of the letter with its inclosure had heen forwarded to Rear-Admiral W. S.
                    Schley.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John D. Long.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
